# Landing chrome everywhere

Always use `LandingNavbar` and `LandingFooter` (via `MarketingShell`) for public marketing, SEO, legal, and booking surfaces — not `BrandLogo` / the old marketing header/footer.

- Prefer `MarketingShell` for shared public pages (home, pricing, cleaning, cleaners, FAQ, for-cleaners, how-it-works, privacy, cookies, terms).
- Do not reintroduce a separate marketing nav/footer with different logo fonts or layout.
- App shells (customer/cleaner/admin dashboards) keep their own chrome; public-facing pages use the landing chrome.
